    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. just to clarify, regarding the insurance part—is the seller required to provide a specific level of coverage, or can they just pick whatever minimum is standard? i dont want us to be stuck with a crappy policy if the semiconductors get damaged in transit.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF, the seller is required to keep the goods insured until they are discharged from the vessel at the destination port. Additionally, Incoterms 2020 Clause 5 states that the seller's insurance coverage must \"cover all risks of loss or damage (other than those caused by or incurred by the buyer\" This means that the seller should provide insurance coverage that meets the minimum requirements, and ideally, the policy should be specifically tailored to the goods being shipped (in this case, semiconductors).",
      "source": "target",
